No. The rate limit does not block `/health`.

The nginx config in `projects/drawmatic/DEPLOYMENT.md` applies `limit_req` to two location blocks only:

- `location /api/` → `limit_req zone=api burst=20 nodelay;` (10 r/s per IP)
- `location /api/upload` → `limit_req zone=upload burst=5 nodelay;` (2 r/s per IP)

The `/health` endpoint is a separate location block with no `limit_req` directive:

```nginx
location /health {
    access_log off;
    return 200 "healthy\n";
    add_header Content-Type text/plain;
}
```

nginx matches `/health` to the `location /health` prefix block, not to `location /api/`. The rate limit zones (`limit_req_zone`) only define the zones. The `limit_req` directive enforces them, and it appears in no block that `/health` matches. No server-level or http-level `limit_req` exists either.

Your uptime monitor hits `/health` every 10 seconds (0.1 r/s). It never touches the rate-limited paths. It will not get a 429.

